# SEO and meta

Full contract: [`docs/specs/spec-seo-meta.md`](docs/specs/spec-seo-meta.md).

## When you add or edit a public page

1. Put **title, description, path, OG image, keyword clusters** in `lib/seo-page-meta.ts` (`pageSeo`).
2. In the route file, export `metadataFromPageSeo(pageSeo.<id>)` only. Do not copy title strings into the page.
3. Indexable pages get canonical + `openGraph` + Twitter via `shareMetadata`. Auth pages: `index: false`.

## Titles and descriptions

- Write like a person, not a keyword template. Mix openers (question, promise, contrast). Do **not** start every title with the same phrase.
- Home and course may lead with **intent-driven engineering** / **intent-driven engineer**. Other URLs can lead with SDD, Spec Kit, Jira, videos, etc.
- **Title:** one glanceable line, **50–58 characters** (`SEO_TITLE_MIN`–`SEO_TITLE_MAX`). **Ends with a period.** No brand suffix. Auth pages (`/sign-in`, `/account`) are **`noindex`**: still end with a period and use **Intent-Driven Community** in title and description; the 50–58 / 140–155 rules do not apply.
- **Description:** **140–155 characters** (`SEO_DESC_MIN`–`SEO_DESC_MAX`). One thought that matches the title. Not a comma-separated keyword list.
- Sentence case; named terms stay (**SDD**, **Spec Kit**, **OpenSpec**, **Kiro**).
- Post `heading` / `name` can stay reader-facing; `title` and `description` are the search snippet.

## Keywords

Clusters live in `lib/seo-keywords.ts` (`sddCore`, `intent`, `ticketsAndSpecs`, `practice`, `tools`, `agents`, `course`, `ecosystem`).

- One URL, **one or two primary clusters**.
- New blog post: add `clustersForPostSlug` plus frontmatter `title` / `description` / `socialImage`.
- Do not stuff the homepage or body with every cluster.

## Images

- Default share art: `siteConfig.defaultShareImage` (`/images/og-home.png`). Hub pages use `/images/og-*.png` (**16:9**, 1280×720). Never use the logo as `og:image`.
- Blog: `socialImage` → first local body image → `/images/og-default.png`.

## Do not

- Duplicate meta objects in `page.tsx` when `pageSeo` already has them.
- Create thin tag/keyword URLs (see Phase 2 in the spec).
- Keyword-stuff H1s or in-article links.
